; Leg EB -- THE HEADLINE.  Same leg as EA, one binary over.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
;  Binary under test: D:\CKFNF.EXE, md5 039fae2a..., edits 23-26.
;
;  PREDICTION, fixed before the run:
;      EA - EB  >=  2.0 s          (SS16bc priced zchko at 4.404 s on a
;                                   156-entry root; this one has 184)
;      dec max  450 -> ~100-150 at #3
;      byte-exact, rxlost=0 rxfull=0, wire bytes IDENTICAL to EA
;
;  If the wire bytes differ from EA, the legs are not comparable and the
;  clock difference means nothing -- read the wire before the clock.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPEB.OUT> s16bdEB.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 9600
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bdEB.pkt
send rcveb.dat
statistics
